From 2568d682343fc0f6c9e7695d1fe9067faeb95bec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teja Kota <krishnatejakota@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:31:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] product_film: give the film a camera, cuts, and a caret that
 lands
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The film had no motion vocabulary. Eighty-six `Opacity` wrappers, one
`translate`, no `Transform` at all; fifty `ease_out_cubic` against two
`ease_in_out`, so nothing ever accelerated and therefore nothing ever
left. Measured as mean inter-frame difference the whole picture runs at
about 0.03/255 — eighteen thousand frames rendered to deliver a sequence
of stills. This adds the parts that were missing and fixes the
arithmetic that was wrong.

The caret. Three faults at once: the type-on text was centred in a
full-width box, so it re-centred on every keystroke while the caret was
pinned to a point derived from the finished line (about 190 px adrift at
the start); `gmono_w` ignored `letter_spacing`; and the end card's
release line is proportional Geist measured with a monospace advance,
which no constant can fix. `vieww-text`'s own test says it — "measuring
one way and drawing another puts the caret between the wrong letters" —
so nothing estimates any more: `measured_caret` lays the run out through
the film's own `FontStore` and asks `Paragraph::cursor_rect`.

The band. Narration shared the bottom third with the distance readout
and, in the studio act, the app's own tab bar, with nothing reserving a
lane. The film now keeps a strip at the top for its own voice, oldest
line highest, newest at full weight. The readout stays at the bottom,
alone. "every number on screen is a receipt — counted, not claimed" is
no longer truncated at "n".

The camera. `Scene::append` lifts the frame's command list into another
space without replaying paint, the same seam `SCALE_FACTOR` rides. B03
dives into the glyph (its own module doc always said it did); D02
finally pulls back. Movement III holds `Cam::STILL` — a scaled frame is
resampled pixels and that act's claim is that they are the product's
own. Chrome registers in screen space and composites after the camera,
so the captions stay put while the picture moves.

The cut. Every scene enters decelerating and leaves accelerating, with a
luminance ramp riding along; the +22.5-in-one-frame jump into the studio
act is gone.

Depth. `panel_3d` uses `Transform3` for an exact projected silhouette
with a fitted affine for the contents (approximate, and said so where it
is). Stars and dust get strata.

Fixed on the way: `band_scrim` painted from the size handed in rather
than its own, laying a near-opaque gradient over all 1080 rows and
dropping the studio to a third of its luminance; every chip row
overlapped its neighbour and the readout spilled "ms" out of its pill,
both from the missing tracking term; A04's device labels sat a whole
device-height below the devices they name; the studio headline was
painted through lines 4-8 of the code in all nine scenes, and the
receipt rows through the preview pane's paragraph; `work_root` was an
absolute path into one machine's home directory, which made the
documented review loop unrunnable anywhere else.

Verified by rendering 16 of 23 scenes and looking at them. Not verified:
this bench has no rustc 1.98.1, so C05-C09's real compile pipeline did
not run. `censuspf` needs re-running — the command counts moved.

